From: Nickolay Semendyaev <agent00791@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] surfaceflinger: a narrow panel still deserves its colours

populateColorModes returns early for a display without a wide gamut,
which leaves the colour mode table empty -- and with an empty table
the colour setting has nothing to pick from, so a narrow panel is
locked to native no matter what the composer offers. But nothing in
the SDR half of that table needs a wide panel: sRGB and native modes
with their render intents describe an sRGB-class display exactly as
well, and the composer behind it maps every intent onto its own
colour machinery. The SDR half is now built for every display; the
HDR half keeps the original gate.

Rebased for Q. The code is unchanged in substance but has moved out of
DisplayDevice into the composition engine: DisplayColorProfile owns the
table now, and the argument is spelled DisplayColorProfileCreationArgs::
HwcColorModes rather than the bare map. The early return survived the
move untouched, so the fix is the same one, in its new house.

diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/DisplayColorProfile.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/DisplayColorProfile.cpp
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/DisplayColorProfile.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/DisplayColorProfile.cpp
@@ -271,9 +271,12 @@

 void DisplayColorProfile::populateColorModes(
         const DisplayColorProfileCreationArgs::HwcColorModes& hwcColorModes) {
-    if (!hasWideColorGamut()) {
-        return;
-    }
+    // The SDR half of the table is built for every display. Upstream
+    // returns early for a narrow-gamut panel, which leaves the table
+    // empty and the colour setting with nothing to pick from -- but
+    // nothing below this line needs a wide panel: sRGB and native
+    // modes with their render intents describe an sRGB-class display
+    // exactly as well. The HDR half keeps the original gate.

     // collect all known SDR render intents
     std::unordered_set<RenderIntent> sdrRenderIntents(sSdrRenderIntents.begin(),
@@ -292,6 +295,10 @@
         }
     }

+    if (!hasWideColorGamut()) {
+        return;
+    }
+
     // collect all known HDR render intents
     std::unordered_set<RenderIntent> hdrRenderIntents(sHdrRenderIntents.begin(),
                                                       sHdrRenderIntents.end());
